<title>USA: Marshall &amp; Ilsley Corp Q4 net up.</title>
<headline>Marshall &amp; Ilsley Corp Q4 net up.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.63		    $0.53</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$0.62		    $0.51</p>
<p> Net			 61,869		   52,348</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>		 YEAR</p>
<p> Shr primary		$2.07		    $1.96</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$2.02		    $1.90</p>
<p> Net			203,430		  193,299</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 full year results include special charges taken in the Q3 related to the acquisition of EastPoint Technology Inc. The corporation wrote off $12.1 million ($7.9 million after tax or $0.08/shr) of research and development costs. It also accrued $2.8 million ($1.8 million after tax or $0.02/shr) for the special assessment associated with SAIF deposits.</p>
<p>Assets at yearend were $14.8 billion vs $13.3 billion in 1995. ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
